NUM-34: give [GWF] expressions K(theta), not the percolation rate

6.0.0 sets the variable K of custom groundwater flow expressions to the
upper-zone percolation rate (0 below field capacity, and including the
tension gradient and the cap above it). The input reference defines K as the
unsaturated hydraulic conductivity, K(theta) = Ks exp(-(phi - theta) HCO),
which is what 5.3.0 computes (and, with NUM-34_swmm530.patch, computes for
every aquifer). Use that value in both the DEEP and the LATERAL expression.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-34_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Groundwater.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Groundwater.cpp
index 9611079..6fde08d 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/Groundwater.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/Groundwater.cpp
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@ static void getFluxes(GWContext& c, double theta, double lower_depth) {
         vars[GWV_HCB]   = c.h_star * c.ucf_length;
         vars[GWV_HGS]   = c.total_depth * c.ucf_length;
         vars[GWV_KS]    = c.k_sat * c.ucf_rainfall;
-        vars[GWV_K]     = c.upper_perc > 0.0 ? c.upper_perc * c.ucf_rainfall : 0.0;
+        vars[GWV_K]     = c.k_sat * std::exp((theta - c.porosity) * c.k_slope) * c.ucf_rainfall;
         vars[GWV_THETA] = theta;
         vars[GWV_PHI]   = c.porosity;
         vars[GWV_FI]    = c.infil * c.ucf_rainfall;
@@ -214,7 +214,7 @@ static void getFluxes(GWContext& c, double theta, double lower_depth) {
         vars[GWV_HCB]   = c.h_star * c.ucf_length;
         vars[GWV_HGS]   = c.total_depth * c.ucf_length;
         vars[GWV_KS]    = c.k_sat * c.ucf_rainfall;
-        vars[GWV_K]     = c.upper_perc > 0.0 ? c.upper_perc * c.ucf_rainfall : 0.0;
+        vars[GWV_K]     = c.k_sat * std::exp((theta - c.porosity) * c.k_slope) * c.ucf_rainfall;
         vars[GWV_THETA] = theta;
         vars[GWV_PHI]   = c.porosity;
         vars[GWV_FI]    = c.infil * c.ucf_rainfall;
